\newlabel{tab:matrix}{{I}{4}{The run matrix: $130$ evolutions, grouped. Every group varies one knob against a named reference; per-run lines live in the shipped registry. Body parameters are $a=2$, $m=1$ ($R_{\min }=3.89$), $\sigma =-1$, $d=12$ and $L=64$ unless stated. Left: the single throat, the pair and the head-on, with the controls. Right: the orbital family}{table.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks the branch. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4: the exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted), held until each grid's own truncation noise excites the unstable mode---level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the \emph  {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends; muted lines carry the last reading (the level-3 run continues to $t=100$ behind a trapped surface). (b)~The deviation is a single exponential mode with a level-dependent sign: plateau fits give $\tau =5.88$/$5.26$ at levels 3/4, in the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band~\cite  {gonzalez2009}. (c)~Level 3 with the seed \emph  {declared}, Eq.~\eqref  {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward. The fate is opposite to the push, the twins cross at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$, and a tenfold smaller kick arrives $8$--$14$ units later depending on the marker. Burgundy: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$; cross: death at $t=40.1$.}}{4}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single_throat}{{1}{4}{The lone throat is unstable; unless the seed is declared, the grid picks the branch. (a)~Minimal areal radius from exact static data at refinement levels 2--4: the exact solution is a fixed point ($R_\star $, dotted), held until each grid's own truncation noise excites the unstable mode---level 3 (dashed) collapses, level 4 (solid) inflates, level 2 (grey) dies of an origin failure first (cross). Dots mark where the \emph {scan} loses the throat, not where the run ends; muted lines carry the last reading (the level-3 run continues to $t=100$ behind a trapped surface). (b)~The deviation is a single exponential mode with a level-dependent sign: plateau fits give $\tau =5.88$/$5.26$ at levels 3/4, in the Gonz\'alez--Guzm\'an--Sarbach band~\cite {gonzalez2009}. (c)~Level 3 with the seed \emph {declared}, Eq.~\eqref {eq:seed}: $\varepsilon =\pm 10^{-2}$ (heavy), $\pm 10^{-3}$ (light); dashed = outward. The fate is opposite to the push, the twins cross at the $\varepsilon $-independent $t_\times \simeq 13.0$, and a tenfold smaller kick arrives $8$--$14$ units later depending on the marker. Burgundy: exponential fits $|R-R_\star |\propto e^{t/\tau }$; cross: death at $t=40.1$}{figure.1}{}}
