\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The head-on merger makes a black hole ($d=8$ from rest, opposite scalar signs); every horizon point is the orientation-corrected scan. (a)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits: level 3 carries the approach from $d=7.94$ (the tracker's grid snap on a true $8$); the common MOTS forms at $t=22$ (burgundy rule in every time panel), the scout dies at the level-3 wall at $t=26.91$ (dashed rule), and the level-5 arm, restarted at $t=22$ with every interior device off, carries the merged pit to $t=100$ with no NaN. (b)~The minimum lapse (level 5, ink) rides the $10^{-10}$ clamp over $t=38.5$--$41.0$ and settles at $1.1\times 10^{-3}$. (c)~Minimum $\chi $: excursions onto the $10^{-20}$ clamp leave the frame; level 5 returns and settles at $2.0\times 10^{-5}$. (d)~The wall is resolution: $\max |K|$ blows up to $18$ at the level-3 death; level 5 never exceeds $1.34$ and ends at $0.14$. (e)~The scout's $\|\mathcal  {H}\|$ explodes at the wall ($13.6$); the level-5 norms fall $4.6\times 10^{-3}\to 1.4\times 10^{-3}$; the down-step (level 3 again, from the $t=35$ checkpoint) lands on them to median $0.08\%/1.5\%$. (f)~The horizon: filled diamonds, offline scans at $\mathrm  {d}x=0.0625$ (formation at $t=22$, $r=3.17$, $R=5.56$; growth to $5.71$ by $t=24$; then $4.72$, and $4.92/4.87$ at $t=42.5/43$); open circles, the live scan on three arms. Its gaps are aperture, not horizon loss---the shells reach $0.5\,d+2.3$, so once the pits merge the surface at $r\simeq 2.7$--$3.3$ lies outside while every shell within reports trapped; where two arms see it at once they agree ($t=36$: $R=4.461$ against $4.441$). (g)~The Misner--Sharp mass drifts down, $2.99$ at formation to $2.17$ at $t=99$ ($-0.0066$ per unit fitted on the down-step track): phantom infall \emph  {removes} mass. (h)~Expansions at the areal minimum: $\theta _+$ crosses zero between $t=20$ and $21$, both negative by $t=24$; the per-mouth scans never find an own MOTS---the horizon is born common. (i)~The field's extrema fall $\pm 0.86\to \pm 0.008$ with $|\Pi |\le 0.07$: the supporting scalar is swallowed and radiated, leaving vacuum around a black hole. (j)~The remnant's $(2,0)$ mode at $R=10$ rings with period ${\sim }31$--$38$, $\times 0.6$--$0.8$ per half-swing, as the mass in (g) declines.}}{8}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headon_collapse}{{4}{8}{The head-on merger makes a black hole ($d=8$ from rest, opposite scalar signs); every horizon point is the orientation-corrected scan. (a)~Separation of the $\chi $ pits: level 3 carries the approach from $d=7.94$ (the tracker's grid snap on a true $8$); the common MOTS forms at $t=22$ (burgundy rule in every time panel), the scout dies at the level-3 wall at $t=26.91$ (dashed rule), and the level-5 arm, restarted at $t=22$ with every interior device off, carries the merged pit to $t=100$ with no NaN. (b)~The minimum lapse (level 5, ink) rides the $10^{-10}$ clamp over $t=38.5$--$41.0$ and settles at $1.1\times 10^{-3}$. (c)~Minimum $\chi $: excursions onto the $10^{-20}$ clamp leave the frame; level 5 returns and settles at $2.0\times 10^{-5}$. (d)~The wall is resolution: $\max |K|$ blows up to $18$ at the level-3 death; level 5 never exceeds $1.34$ and ends at $0.14$. (e)~The scout's $\|\mathcal {H}\|$ explodes at the wall ($13.6$); the level-5 norms fall $4.6\times 10^{-3}\to 1.4\times 10^{-3}$; the down-step (level 3 again, from the $t=35$ checkpoint) lands on them to median $0.08\%/1.5\%$. (f)~The horizon: filled diamonds, offline scans at $\mathrm {d}x=0.0625$ (formation at $t=22$, $r=3.17$, $R=5.56$; growth to $5.71$ by $t=24$; then $4.72$, and $4.92/4.87$ at $t=42.5/43$); open circles, the live scan on three arms. Its gaps are aperture, not horizon loss---the shells reach $0.5\,d+2.3$, so once the pits merge the surface at $r\simeq 2.7$--$3.3$ lies outside while every shell within reports trapped; where two arms see it at once they agree ($t=36$: $R=4.461$ against $4.441$). (g)~The Misner--Sharp mass drifts down, $2.99$ at formation to $2.17$ at $t=99$ ($-0.0066$ per unit fitted on the down-step track): phantom infall \emph {removes} mass. (h)~Expansions at the areal minimum: $\theta _+$ crosses zero between $t=20$ and $21$, both negative by $t=24$; the per-mouth scans never find an own MOTS---the horizon is born common. (i)~The field's extrema fall $\pm 0.86\to \pm 0.008$ with $|\Pi |\le 0.07$: the supporting scalar is swallowed and radiated, leaving vacuum around a black hole. (j)~The remnant's $(2,0)$ mode at $R=10$ rings with period ${\sim }31$--$38$, $\times 0.6$--$0.8$ per half-swing, as the mass in (g) declines}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The production spiral's collapse ($p=0.12$, $d=12$): the level-5 window from the restart at $t=36$ to the death by NaN at $t=60.44$, all of it unfrozen physics---the interior fill plays no part in any panel. (a)~Coordinate separation of the two $\chi $ pits over the whole history: the level-3 leg carries the plunge from $d=11.9$ to the handover at $t=36$ (solid rule); the constraint transient at $t=41.2$ (dashed rule here and in every time panel) marks the merger, after which the tracker follows a single merged pit (pale); the record ends at the NaN. (b)~The minimum lapse bottoms at $2.0\times 10^{-3}$ and never reaches zero. (c)~The minimum conformal factor decays exponentially and sits on the code's $10^{-8}$ floor from $t=58.43$ (dotted rule in every time panel), at $r=0.078$. (d)~The scalar field's extrema hold $\pm 0.89$ throughout while its momentum saturates at $\Pi =\pm 4.1$: the profile survives, the momentum diverges. (e)~Growth compared, each curve $\log _{10}$-scaled onto $[0,1]$: the constraint norms peak at the merger and relax below where they started, while $\max |K|$ only begins its climb near $t=49$---after $t=40$, $\mathrm  {corr}(\log \max |K|,\log \|\mathcal  {H}\|)=-0.35$ and $\mathrm  {corr}(\log \max |K|,\log \|\mathcal  {M}\|)=+0.04$, so the death is not a constraint blow-up. The pale curves are the level-3 leg's norms through the same transforms: they lie on the level-5 curves to a median $3.5\%$ ($\mathcal  {H}$) and $0.7\%$ ($\mathcal  {M}$) over the shared window $t=36$--$50$---the transient is resolved, not resolution. (f)~Where the curvature wall lives: the radius of the $|K|$ spike (steps; drawn from $t=49.1$, before which the profile is flat and an argmax is noise) and the disturbance's outer edge $|K|>0.2$ (dashed), widest at $r=1.36$ ($t=51.4$) and contracting after. Burgundy circles: the throat's coordinate radius from the orientation-corrected marginal-surface scans---the spike rides just outside the throat and lands on it by the death. (g)~The same scans' throat areal radius: $R$ shrinks $4.10\to 3.87$ ($-5.7\%$) over $t=55$--$60$, levels 3 and 5 agreeing to $0.2\%$, and \emph  {no} marginally outer-trapped surface exists at any scan---the collapse runs to the end with no horizon found. (The in-code $\theta _+$ columns are not drawn: their naive $+r$ orientation manufactures trapped verdicts near a throat, the artefact behind a withdrawn early horizon claim.) (h)--(j)~The radial anatomy at six equally spaced times, light ($t=36.1$) to dark ($t=60.4$): the per-shell $\max |K|$ grows $0.08\to 6.1$ on a spike ${\sim }0.25$ wide migrating inward (h), while the $\chi $ pit (i) and the lapse pit (j) stay at $r\lesssim 0.15$. The gauge collapse and the curvature wall are different places: the pit at the centre, the wall on the throat.}}{9}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spiral_collapse}{{5}{9}{The production spiral's collapse ($p=0.12$, $d=12$): the level-5 window from the restart at $t=36$ to the death by NaN at $t=60.44$, all of it unfrozen physics---the interior fill plays no part in any panel. (a)~Coordinate separation of the two $\chi $ pits over the whole history: the level-3 leg carries the plunge from $d=11.9$ to the handover at $t=36$ (solid rule); the constraint transient at $t=41.2$ (dashed rule here and in every time panel) marks the merger, after which the tracker follows a single merged pit (pale); the record ends at the NaN. (b)~The minimum lapse bottoms at $2.0\times 10^{-3}$ and never reaches zero. (c)~The minimum conformal factor decays exponentially and sits on the code's $10^{-8}$ floor from $t=58.43$ (dotted rule in every time panel), at $r=0.078$. (d)~The scalar field's extrema hold $\pm 0.89$ throughout while its momentum saturates at $\Pi =\pm 4.1$: the profile survives, the momentum diverges. (e)~Growth compared, each curve $\log _{10}$-scaled onto $[0,1]$: the constraint norms peak at the merger and relax below where they started, while $\max |K|$ only begins its climb near $t=49$---after $t=40$, $\mathrm {corr}(\log \max |K|,\log \|\mathcal {H}\|)=-0.35$ and $\mathrm {corr}(\log \max |K|,\log \|\mathcal {M}\|)=+0.04$, so the death is not a constraint blow-up. The pale curves are the level-3 leg's norms through the same transforms: they lie on the level-5 curves to a median $3.5\%$ ($\mathcal {H}$) and $0.7\%$ ($\mathcal {M}$) over the shared window $t=36$--$50$---the transient is resolved, not resolution. (f)~Where the curvature wall lives: the radius of the $|K|$ spike (steps; drawn from $t=49.1$, before which the profile is flat and an argmax is noise) and the disturbance's outer edge $|K|>0.2$ (dashed), widest at $r=1.36$ ($t=51.4$) and contracting after. Burgundy circles: the throat's coordinate radius from the orientation-corrected marginal-surface scans---the spike rides just outside the throat and lands on it by the death. (g)~The same scans' throat areal radius: $R$ shrinks $4.10\to 3.87$ ($-5.7\%$) over $t=55$--$60$, levels 3 and 5 agreeing to $0.2\%$, and \emph {no} marginally outer-trapped surface exists at any scan---the collapse runs to the end with no horizon found. (The in-code $\theta _+$ columns are not drawn: their naive $+r$ orientation manufactures trapped verdicts near a throat, the artefact behind a withdrawn early horizon claim.) (h)--(j)~The radial anatomy at six equally spaced times, light ($t=36.1$) to dark ($t=60.4$): the per-shell $\max |K|$ grows $0.08\to 6.1$ on a spike ${\sim }0.25$ wide migrating inward (h), while the $\chi $ pit (i) and the lapse pit (j) stay at $r\lesssim 0.15$. The gauge collapse and the curvature wall are different places: the pit at the centre, the wall on the throat}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The wall does not move: death time of the $p=0.12$ spiral against refinement, every arm restarted from the same $t=50$ checkpoint, every death an $h_{11}$ NaN, no horizon at any rung. Filled: plain evolution, per-doubling gains marked. Open diamond: the level-5 arm at half the time step. Open circles: the core-damping family---a different treatment, dying on the same clock. Faint rule: the production chain (doubled base grid, restart at $t=36$), $4.2$ units past the whole ladder and still short of the merger's end.}}{10}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spiral_ladder}{{6}{10}{The wall does not move: death time of the $p=0.12$ spiral against refinement, every arm restarted from the same $t=50$ checkpoint, every death an $h_{11}$ NaN, no horizon at any rung. Filled: plain evolution, per-doubling gains marked. Open diamond: the level-5 arm at half the time step. Open circles: the core-damping family---a different treatment, dying on the same clock. Faint rule: the production chain (doubled base grid, restart at $t=36$), $4.2$ units past the whole ladder and still short of the merger's end}{figure.6}{}}
