\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces The waveform gallery: every channel's radiation, one row per scenario, one retarded clock. Left column: $r\,\mathrm  {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost extraction sphere, each row on its own stated scale---the lone throat radiates an order of magnitude below the mergers, and the fly-by is the loudest channel of all. Half-height caps mark record ends: the collapsing throat's stream is junk-gated at $t=70$, the spiral record ends at $t=60$ with the run still in flight, and the fly-by---complete to $t=100$, no horizon ever forming---is gated at $t=70$, ahead of the $t=76.1$ trough where the mouths' expansion (areal radii growing $\times 7.8$) has grown to equal the decaying burst at the $R=20$ sphere. Right column: the envelope $|r\Psi _4|$ at every extraction sphere on its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer): a signal travelling at $c$ and falling as $1/r$ folds onto one curve. Burgundy dots mark the correlated wavefront, and the quoted $v/c$ is the lag of the whole complex waveform between neighbouring spheres over their common retarded window---peak-to-peak timing fails on flat-topped envelopes (the vacuum twin's merger plateau is ${\sim }15$ units wide at both spheres, and its peak times alone would read $v=0.57c$ where the waveform lag reads $0.82c$). Measured speeds: throat $0.91/0.95/0.98$, head-on $0.96/0.90$, spiral $0.95/1.00/1.00$, fly-by $1.00/1.00/1.00$, vacuum twin $0.82$. Every channel propagates at $c$ within the output cadence: radiation, not a gauge or constraint mode.}}{11}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_gallery}{{7}{11}{The waveform gallery: every channel's radiation, one row per scenario, one retarded clock. Left column: $r\,\mathrm {Re}\,\Psi _4$ of the dominant mode at the innermost extraction sphere, each row on its own stated scale---the lone throat radiates an order of magnitude below the mergers, and the fly-by is the loudest channel of all. Half-height caps mark record ends: the collapsing throat's stream is junk-gated at $t=70$, the spiral record ends at $t=60$ with the run still in flight, and the fly-by---complete to $t=100$, no horizon ever forming---is gated at $t=70$, ahead of the $t=76.1$ trough where the mouths' expansion (areal radii growing $\times 7.8$) has grown to equal the decaying burst at the $R=20$ sphere. Right column: the envelope $|r\Psi _4|$ at every extraction sphere on its own retarded time (ink to faint, inner to outer): a signal travelling at $c$ and falling as $1/r$ folds onto one curve. Burgundy dots mark the correlated wavefront, and the quoted $v/c$ is the lag of the whole complex waveform between neighbouring spheres over their common retarded window---peak-to-peak timing fails on flat-topped envelopes (the vacuum twin's merger plateau is ${\sim }15$ units wide at both spheres, and its peak times alone would read $v=0.57c$ where the waveform lag reads $0.82c$). Measured speeds: throat $0.91/0.95/0.98$, head-on $0.96/0.90$, spiral $0.95/1.00/1.00$, fly-by $1.00/1.00/1.00$, vacuum twin $0.82$. Every channel propagates at $c$ within the output cadence: radiation, not a gauge or constraint mode}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Every source on a detector at one shared calibration: total mass $M=30\,M_\odot $, distance $D=10$ Mpc, each record first reduced to units of its own total ADM mass; strain scales as $M/D$, frequency as $1/M$. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere on a common merger clock ($\tau =0$ at each peak): fly-by loudest ($8.2\times 10^{-2}$), then spiral, head-on, vacuum twin, lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (burgundy), each curve drawn from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked), below which a record of length $T$ cannot tell a wave from a drift. Read them as falling power laws (slopes $-3.3$ to $-5.9$) with no resolved maximum: any ``peak'' taken from this panel is the corner $1/T$; the values at the resolved $\Psi _4$ peaks are quoted in the text. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde  h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz---the ramp an astrophysical binary rides into the band where the simulated signal begins. (c)~Instantaneous frequency over each record's body against the point-mass chirp (burgundy), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$, the textbook merger value; no wormhole channel does (tracks in Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole, ranked; the tick on each bar is the spread over extraction spheres, the error bar that catches near-zone content posing as a wave (fly-by $43\%$, the widest: the expansion of its open mouths is near-zone content the outer spheres see less of). Open burgundy bars: the published equal-mass vacuum results from rest at infinity---head-on infall $5.5\times 10^{-4}$, quasi-circular merger $4.84\times 10^{-2}$---which bracket any vacuum binary; the spiral and fly-by outradiate the vacuum twin by $8.5\times $ and $29\times $. Energies are band integrals of $|\DOTSI \intop \ilimits@ r\Psi _4\,\mathrm  {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for the $\pm m$ pair; gravitational channel only---the scalar's own energy is invisible to $\Psi _4$.}}{12}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gw_ligo}{{8}{12}{Every source on a detector at one shared calibration: total mass $M=30\,M_\odot $, distance $D=10$ Mpc, each record first reduced to units of its own total ADM mass; strain scales as $M/D$, frequency as $1/M$. (a)~Envelopes $|r\Psi _4|M$ at the innermost sphere on a common merger clock ($\tau =0$ at each peak): fly-by loudest ($8.2\times 10^{-2}$), then spiral, head-on, vacuum twin, lone throat ($3.1\times 10^{-3}$). (b)~Strain amplitude spectral densities over the aLIGO design floor (burgundy), each curve drawn from its own low-frequency corner (one cycle per record, ticked), below which a record of length $T$ cannot tell a wave from a drift. Read them as falling power laws (slopes $-3.3$ to $-5.9$) with no resolved maximum: any ``peak'' taken from this panel is the corner $1/T$; the values at the resolved $\Psi _4$ peaks are quoted in the text. Faint line: the Newtonian inspiral of the same binary, $|\tilde h|\propto f^{-7/6}$ to its ISCO at $147$ Hz---the ramp an astrophysical binary rides into the band where the simulated signal begins. (c)~Instantaneous frequency over each record's body against the point-mass chirp (burgundy), the ISCO ($147$ Hz) and the equal-mass Kerr ringdown ($599$ Hz): the vacuum twin climbs the chirp and peaks at $fM=0.065$, the textbook merger value; no wormhole channel does (tracks in Sec.~\ref {sec:ligo:ringdown}). (d)~Energy radiated in the dominant multipole, ranked; the tick on each bar is the spread over extraction spheres, the error bar that catches near-zone content posing as a wave (fly-by $43\%$, the widest: the expansion of its open mouths is near-zone content the outer spheres see less of). Open burgundy bars: the published equal-mass vacuum results from rest at infinity---head-on infall $5.5\times 10^{-4}$, quasi-circular merger $4.84\times 10^{-2}$---which bracket any vacuum binary; the spiral and fly-by outradiate the vacuum twin by $8.5\times $ and $29\times $. Energies are band integrals of $|\int r\Psi _4\,\mathrm {d}t'|^2$ over a common retarded window, doubled for the $\pm m$ pair; gravitational channel only---the scalar's own energy is invisible to $\Psi _4$}{figure.8}{}}
